/*Simplified Equation for math dumb-dumbs like me for calculating Width Height based on Original Sprite vs Target Size in game

Simplified Equation
For any given original size (in units 64 = 1 unit) ["𝑊orig","𝐻orig"] and target width "𝑊target":

𝐻target = "𝐻orig" * ("𝑊target" / "𝑊orig")
​
Explanation
Original Width (𝑊orig): The width of the sprite in its original form.
Original Height (𝐻orig): The height of the sprite in its original form.
Target Width (𝑊target: The width you WANT the sprite to be.
Target Height (𝐻target): The height the sprite SHOULD be, calculated to maintain the aspect ratio.

Example: I have a sprite that is originally [5, 7] I want it to be width of 2 units wide.
Original Width (𝑊orig): 5
Original Height (𝐻orig): 7
Target Width (𝑊target: 2
Target Height (𝐻target): "T" (Target)

T = 7 * (2 / 5) = 2.8 New Size = [2, 2.8]

*/
		EngineRoofDoodadsOptionToggle0
		{
			Type = ModeToggle
			Mode = EngineRoofDoodadsOptionToggle
			OnMode = 0
		}
		
		EngineRoofDoodadsOptionToggle1
		{
			Type = ModeToggle
			Mode = EngineRoofDoodadsOptionToggle
			OnMode = 1
		}
		EngineRoofDoodadsComponents1
		{
			Type = ToggledComponents
			Toggle = EngineRoofDoodadsOptionToggle1
			//Invert = true
			Components
			{
				EngineRoofDoodadsGraphics1
				{
					Type = Graphics
					Location = [5, 14]
					Roof
					{
						Layer = "SW.roof_engines"
						Offset = [0, -11.5]//
						DamageLevels
						[
							{
								File = "../Ion_Common/Nozzle_Covers/MED/nozzle_cover_roof_11.png"
								NormalsFile =  "../Ion_Common/Nozzle_Covers/MED/nozzle_cover_roof_10_normals.png"
								Size = [13, 28] 
								//UVRotation = 2
							}
						]
					}
				}
			}
		}

